# Airflow DAG-discovery ignore list (default regexp syntax).
#
# Patterns are Python regex, matched with re.search against each path RELATIVE
# to this file's directory (the registered bundle root = repo root). If a path
# matches any line, Airflow's scanner will NOT parse it as a DAG file.
#
# Why this exists: Airflow's safe-mode scanner imports any *.py containing both
# the substrings "airflow" and "dag" as a standalone module. For library code
# that uses relative imports (e.g. ftp_handler/direct_downloader/collect.py),
# that standalone import fails with:
#     ImportError: attempted relative import with no known parent package
# These packages are meant to be IMPORTED at runtime, never parsed as DAGs.
#
# The ONLY directory holding real DAGs is airflow_mgmt/dags/ — everything else
# below is ignored.

# ── Top-level first-party packages (importable libs, not DAGs) ───────────────
^ftp_handler/
^ops_store/
^minio_handler/
^ops_index_mgmt/
^url_shortner/
^api/
^tests/
^utils/

# ── Non-DAG folders inside airflow_mgmt/ (keep dags/ scanned) ────────────────
^airflow_mgmt/dag_templates/
^airflow_mgmt/scripts/
^airflow_mgmt/templates/
^airflow_mgmt/tests/
^airflow_mgmt/utils/
^airflow_mgmt/minio_handler/
^airflow_mgmt/docs/
